.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-RESET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-reset - Restore the default Inbox directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox reset [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore the default receiving directory, ~/Paperboat/Inbox, for future files. Files already
delivered stay where they are, and the account's team request policy is unchanged. Use
pb inbox set to choose another directory.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reset

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox reset
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
